    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey, i just had to do a rumenotomy on one of my heifers because of a blockage. can u give me a list of what i should be looking for in terms of recovery and signs of infection over the next week? also what should i feed her once she starts acting normal again?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "For recovery, watch for a gradual return to normal appetite and energy levels over the next week. Key signs of infection include increasing fever, severe lethargy, localized heat or swelling at the incision site, and pus discharge. Once she is eating normally, start her on a highly digestible, easily fermentable diet, gradually reintroducing her regular forage to prevent re-bloating. Ensure she has constant access to fresh water during this transition period.",
