      "content": "If you notice persistent signs of heat and redness that don't subside, monitor the incision closely throughout the day rather than just at one time. Pay attention to any discharge that starts changing color or thickening, as this can indicate deeper issues. However, if you suspect the problem is internal or worsening, contacting your veterinarian is the safest course of action for proper assessment, as palpation can be risky.",
